hat are  engaged in a battle for power the power  to exploit and devour other creatures  and even all of creation these creatures  destroy what they did not create and  everywhere they go they are devouring  they are breaking things into pieces  destroying and stamping beneath their  feet what remains homes trees bodies  everything in sight they have they have  human eyes but not human hearts their  eyes see only numbers coordinates and  profit they cannot see people or beauty  or true cost they know no affection no  limits and no loyalty their mouths are  only arrogance Jesus says all of these  things will take place the chaos will  continually increase just as daniel has  dreamt it a chaos that birds these  beastly forms in the world and people  will faint from fear and foreboding and  the very powers of heaven will be  threatened shaken at their core it's  precisely then that Jesus tells us to  stand up with our heads held high as  witnesses to a different truth a  different power a different  for the world we are called to stand up  in this arena of beasts that threaten  permanent night eternal death and  testify to the life and the light that  we find in Christ in this season of  Advent we have been given eyes to see  the places that need God's justice and  God's comfort and God's mercy in the  world we have been given mouths to  truthfully name these things aloud we're  called to call out to others to stand up  and to sit in and solidarity to prepare  the way of the Lord and Jesus assures us  that we will see the Son of man coming  with the clouds this is the fulfillment  of Daniels dream that Christ will claim  full Dominion forever the beasts will  all be laid low the throne has already  been established so even though the sea  has been slapping us around of late even  though there are other nightmares in our  life that haunt us to the point where we  cannot see our way through the next day  the next week the next year we can be  sure sure of Christ promises sure of  Christ Dominion shore of Christ's  salvation for us all we can be so sure  that when we look at the trees they are  barren and nearly dead and yet through  all the months of winter we can wait and  when you see those first buds just  beginning to peek out the shyness of  green and red and white you know then  that spring is surely coming and Jesus  says you can be this Shore and even more  shore because even if the trees should  pass away even if all of creation should  pass away the heavens and the earth  god's word of promise is more solid than  anything that we know anything that we  see anything that we tell  if we should all pass away into darkness  God's Word would remain God's creative  word that said let there be light and  there was light let us rely on that  promise and testify to that light in  this season of Advent amen
 

